hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27672","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad, he said: Haddathana Yazid ibn Ata', from Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas al-Azdi, he said: My mother narrated to me that she saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoning the Jamrat al-Aqabah from the belly of the valley, with a man behind him shielding him from the people lest they hit him with stones, while he was saying: O people, let none of you kill another, and when you stone, stone with pebbles like those of khadhf. Then he came forward, and a woman came to him with a son of hers and said: O Messenger of Allah, this son of mine is bereft of mind, so supplicate Allah for him. He said to her: Bring me water. So she brought him water in a vessel of stone, and he spat in it and washed his face, then supplicated in it, then he said: Go, wash him with it, and seek cure from Allah, mighty and majestic. So I said to her: Give me a little of it for this son of mine. So I took a little of it with my fingers and wiped therewith the side of my son, and he became among the most dutiful of people. Then I asked the woman afterwards what her son did. She said: He healed with the best healing."
"27673","Haddathana Affan, he said: Haddathana Abu Awanah, he said: Haddathana Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas, from his mother, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoning the Jamrat al-Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice from the belly of the valley, while he was saying: O people, let none of you kill another, and when you stone the Jimar, stone with pebbles like those of khadhf. She said: So he threw seven, then he left and did not stand. She said: And behind him was a man shielding him from the people. So I asked about him, and they said: He is al-Fadl ibn Abbas."
